        "original_id": "0e18348f-b34c-5a65-b1b2-553b3a632776",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Loewald, Martin Heidegger\n- Roles: physician, musician, philosopher\n- Places: Germany, Rome University\n- Concepts: language theory, Continental philosophy, philosophical hermeneutics\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Loewald's father died shortly after Hans Loewald's birth and was a Jewish physician interested in dermatology and psychiatry.\n- Hans Loewald's mother was a gifted musician who played the piano.\n- Hans Loewald completed medical training in Germany and also studied philosophy there with Martin Heidegger.\n- Hans Loewald received a medical degree from Rome University in 1935.\n- Martin Heidegger was born on 26 September 1889 and died on 26 May 1976.\n- Martin Heidegger was a German philosopher and a seminal thinker in the Continental tradition and philosophical hermeneutics.\n- Martin Heidegger influenced Hans Loewald through his theory of language.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "26159b68-3056-55e8-854d-6d77ac26dcaa",
        "text": "Page: Hans Loewald. Sentence: Loewald's father, who died shortly after his birth, was a Jewish physician with an interest in dermatology and psychiatry; his mother a gifted musician, who played the piano.\nPage: Hans Loewald. Sentence: Loewald did medical training in Germany - where he also studied philosophy with Martin Heidegger, who would influence him with his theory of language - before taking a medical degree from Rome University in 1935.\nPage: Martin Heidegger. Sentence: Martin Heidegger ( ; ] ; 26 September 188926 May 1976) was a German philosopher and a seminal thinker in the Continental tradition and philosophical hermeneutics.",
